    "statement": "The frozen first-contact-to-E10 envelope |Hy| <= 5 kg m^2/s is the first-binding gate of the production E10 window.  The incoming Hy at physical first contact is 2.947 (fixed by the sealed RES-85 flight handoff; free-flight centroidal angular momentum is conserved), so the whole impact may add at most ~2 units of angular impulse about the SYSTEM_COM.  The vertical arrest requires ~150-175 N*s of vertical impulse within the frozen 10 mm penetration envelope, and every admissible touchdown places the support polygon behind the COM, so the resulting vertical-force lever plus the angled toe-contact horizontal impulse inject more than the available Hy budget.  Within the same support polygon the friction force is one-directional (a rearward force would move the CoP forward of the support), so the controller cannot cancel the injected angular impulse without unloading the feet, which the frozen support-retention gate rejects.",
